 },
 "intro": {
  "title": "THRESHOLD ASCENT",
  "lines": [
   "A city built up a cliff of glass, one tier above another.",
   "The way down is at the top."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "Below the spire is the Deep.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [14, 75],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A gate hall at the foot of a cliff, and the cliff is a city: tiers of terraces up the face, stairs and lifts between them, all of it glass the colour of weak tea."
  },
  {
   "id": "static",
   "at": [14, 72],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "SIGNAL HOUSE",
   "text": "Calder. The lamp is lit. You are breaking up. Say again, Calder."
  },
  {
   "id": "stair",
   "at": [15, 66],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The first stair is under a roof. At the top the terrace is open, and a Warden-Graft with its plate to you will charge down the whole length of it."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate",
   "at": [23, 58],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Run a nail down it: the long number is shorter than it was at the Fields. By about a thousand. I do not know whether that is good news."
  },
  {
   "id": "lift",
   "at": [27, 53],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The lift. A lever on the car sends it up; a call lever on each landing brings it down. Nothing on the next tier can reach you until it is up."
  },
  {
   "id": "second",
   "at": [27, 45],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A shell-back at the foot of the second stair and a singer behind it. They have had a long time to get used to this view. Don't hurry."
  },
  {
   "id": "mother",
   "at": [27, 32],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The third terrace has a mother on it, weeping, and the stone round her is wet. Walk out of what she makes. The lift is on the far side."
  },
  {
   "id": "summit",
   "at": [27, 20],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The top. The whole sea bed behind me, flat to the edge, and the road across it like a scratch. The needles are much nearer from here."
  },
  {
   "id": "note",
   "at": [27, 15],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "A SILENT (NOTE)",
   "text": "Below this is where the count is kept. We go down only to be counted. If you go, you are the first who has not come to be counted."
  },
  {
   "id": "spire",
   "at": [27, 10],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A hollow spire, a round well in the middle of it and a stair going down the wall. Cold air comes up it, and a sound. I think that's what holds the Gate open. I am going down."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [23, 66],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The north wall of the gate hall rings hollow beside the stair."
  }
 ],
